## Frequently asked questions

**Is Aescia ISO 27001 certified?**
Aescia's development practices are aligned to ISO 27001 principles. Formal certification is planned as part of the regulatory and compliance pathway. Sites requiring certification prior to evaluation should raise this in the scoping conversation.

**Does Aescia access or modify patient EMR records?**
No. In the default pilot configuration, Aescia does not connect to or modify patient EMR records. Patient enrolment and clinical actions remain within the site's existing clinical systems.

**What happens to patient data after the pilot ends?**
Data retention and deletion following pilot close is defined in the data governance agreement. Data is deleted at the end of the agreed retention period with documented confirmation.

**Who can access patient data in Aescia?**
Access is role-based and scoped to the pilot. Clinical staff see only their allocated patient cohort. Aescia operational staff have access for platform support and evaluation purposes, subject to confidentiality and data governance obligations.

**Has Aescia been through a penetration test?**
Security testing, including penetration testing, is part of the development and pre-deployment process. Test scope and outcomes are available to sites on request under appropriate information-sharing arrangements.
